From 606e74a5885e953edb8bdbe59deb2131f9fc510e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jetson <jetson@orin-nano.tail52323b.ts.net>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:54:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] nv_attach: map-model prototype fixes after review
 (atomics on local values, lifetime, delivery semantics)

Fixes from a read-only adversarial review of e3f4e18f..c2826dbc (every
finding confirmed by a second reviewer):

- A generic atom/red on a thread-local value is undefined (scalar atom only
  on .global/.shared or generic addresses pointing there, PTX ISA 9.7.15):
  every generic atom/red of a probe function now tests its address with
  isspacep.local; local addresses take a plain load, the operation and a
  store (the memory is the thread's own), others keep the atomic. add, and,
  or, xor, exch and cas, 32 and 64 bits; anything else, or a predicated
  atomic, loads the original module. Check: 64-bit fetch-add, 32-bit add and
  exchange on 1530 values, 0 mismatches over 3.88M thread executions.
- Lifetime: the first device copy of a 1531/1532 map in a process takes a
  reference on the map (never returned, as the array bindings at abrupt
  exit), so a tool's close no longer frees it under the delivery.
- One delivering process per map (status OWNER_PID, taken with a CAS; a
  second live agent gets no device copy, its lookups return NULL).
- The device copy is zeroed on a stream of its own and waited for before
  its address is published (relaxed capture mode).
- Delivery follows the application's synchronizations: hooks on
  cuStreamSynchronize(_ptsz), cuCtxSynchronize(_v2) and cuEventSynchronize
  count them and wake the delivery thread; each delivery reads the count
  before enqueueing its snapshot, so its values hold every add of the
  kernels those synchronizations waited for (PTX ISA 8.9.4, API
  synchronization). Status words: DELIVERIES, EXIT_DELIVERY, OWNER_PID,
  SYNCS_COVERED, SYNCS_AT_EXIT, LAUNCHES_AFTER_LAST_SYNC (one slot per word).
  BPFTIME_GPU_DELIVERY_AT_SYNC=1 delivers inside the synchronize call, so
  the last synchronization is covered before main ends.
- The exit delivery is best effort (CUDA calls after main are undefined by
  the programming guide) and bounded: waits poll cuStreamQuery with a
  deadline (1 s), the delivery thread is never joined while it may be in
  the driver, and a fork child does nothing (owner pid).
- Creation checks for the three types (4-byte keys, entries > 0; 1531/1532
  values in u64 words; 1530 at most 1 KiB, the area at most 1 KiB, else the
  module loads without probes); the direct-run path's bpf_main passes 0 as
  the area; max_entries read as unsigned.

Known, documented: a program that exits without synchronizing after its last
launch loses those launches' adds (the hooks do not note every launch, so
LAUNCHES_AFTER_LAST_SYNC cannot always tell); "atomic adds only" on
1531/1532 is a contract, not checked; several GPU processes per segment
deliver only the first one's values.

